The existing package already has the pinned static XCFramework and reproducible fork tooling, but no named adapter target. I’m adding a dedicated adapter module (the only place importing `ReluxLibSSH2`), wiring it into the macOS provider and harness support, and keeping Core engine-neutral. The implementation will use synchronous libssh2 callbacks backed by bounded async bridges: callbacks return `EAGAIN`, while the serialized actor awaits socket/signing progress and deadlines.
