codex
The named adapter now compiles in isolation. It exposes only Core protocols, records all four deferred semantics as `unsupported`, obtains the raw host key before credential lookup, uses the external signer through an async `EAGAIN` bridge, bounds socket/channel buffers, and routes client rekey/keepalive through libssh2. I’ve also wired the same factory into the macOS provider graph and a dependency-injected harness registration; iOS remains intentionally untouched.
